### CRITICAL

**C1 — Live Neon Postgres password in `.env.local`**
`npg_7be6MwWfSvKa` appears in 8 variables (DATABASE_URL, PGPASSWORD, POSTGRES_PASSWORD…). The file is gitignored but lives on disk in plaintext.
**Action: Rotate the password immediately at console.neon.tech.**

**C2 — Vercel OIDC JWT token in `.vercel/.env.development.local`**
Short-lived (~12h) but regenerated on every `vercel dev` run. The `.vercel/` dir is gitignored — confirm it stays that way.

---

### HIGH

**H1 — Hardcoded n8n webhook URLs as fallback in source code**
`api/drip-signup.js:5` and `api/lead-magnet.js:11-13`:
```js
const N8N_WEBHOOK = process.env.N8N_DRIP_WEBHOOK || 'https://winfredquekoc.app.n8n.cloud/webhook/drip-signup';
```
These are in committed git history. The fallback silently uses the production URL in any environment missing the env var.
**Action:** Remove the hardcoded fallback — throw instead. Enable n8n header-based auth on both webhooks.

**H2 — `isAuthorizedCron` returns `true` when `CRON_SECRET` is unset**
`api/cron/_lib.js:16-21` — Preview deployments (where the secret isn't set) accept every cron request unauthenticated.
**Action:** Flip the default to `return false` or set `CRON_SECRET` in all Vercel environments.

---

### MEDIUM

**M1 — `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *` on `api/drip-signup.js`**
Allows any site to POST PII to this endpoint.
**Action:** Lock to `https://winfredquek.com`.

